    <div class="model-compare reveal-group">
      <div class="os-window reveal">
        <div class="os-titlebar os-titlebar-red">
          <span class="os-title">c4_model.dia</span>
          <span class="os-controls" aria-hidden="true">– ▢ ✕</span>
        </div>
        <div class="os-body">
          <div class="mc-chain">C1 → C2 → C3 → C4</div>
          <h3>C4 — The 4-Corner Model</h3>
          <p class="mc-desc">Pure network exchange: supplier to buyer through two Access Points. The tax authority is not in the flow. This is Peppol's original architecture and still the default across most of the network.</p>
          <ul class="mc-list">
            <li><strong>EU</strong> — BIS Billing 3.0, B2G and growing B2B</li>
            <li><strong>Australia / New Zealand</strong> — PINT A-NZ</li>
            <li><strong>Japan</strong> — PINT JP, Qualified Invoice System</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="os-window reveal">
        <div class="os-titlebar os-titlebar-red">
          <span class="os-title">c5_model.dia</span>
          <span class="os-controls" aria-hidden="true">– ▢ ✕</span>
        </div>
        <div class="os-body">
          <div class="mc-chain">C1 → C2 → C3 → C4<br><span class="mc-c5">↘ C5 Tax Authority ↙</span></div>
          <h3>C5 — The 5-Corner Model</h3>
          <p class="mc-desc">Same exchange, plus a fifth corner: the tax authority receives invoice data continuously from the service providers. Continuous Transaction Controls (CTC) on Peppol rails — the model regulators are converging on.</p>
          <ul class="mc-list">
            <li><strong>Singapore</strong> — IRAS receives GST data via C5 · <a href="/peppol-singapore">Singapore page</a></li>
            <li><strong>UAE</strong> — FTA receives Tax Data Documents via DCTCE · <a href="/peppol-uae">UAE page</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="peppol-explainer reveal-group" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
      <div class="explainer-item reveal">
        <span class="explainer-tag">AS4 Protocol</span>
        <h5>Secure Message Exchange</h5>
        <p>AS4 is the messaging backbone of Peppol — a reliable, signed, encrypted protocol for B2B document transport. All Access Points must implement AS4 to be Peppol-certified.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="explainer-item reveal">
        <span class="explainer-tag">SMP / SML Routing</span>
        <h5>The Peppol DNS Layer</h5>
        <p>SMP stores each participant's capabilities. SML is the central DNS-like registry. Together they enable any C2 Access Point to discover and route to any C3 Access Point globally.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="explainer-item reveal">
        <span class="explainer-tag">Peppol BIS 3.0</span>
        <h5>The Document Standard</h5>
        <p>Peppol BIS Billing 3.0 (aligned with EN16931) is the standard invoice format — based on UBL 2.1 XML with Peppol-specific constraints. Country extensions add local fields.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

